  "description": "`ads.gate_shown` → `ads.result`, by placement and platform (SPEC §14).\n\n**Watch no-fill.** Every no-fill is a reward given away, and SPEC 5.3 says that is the *correct* behaviour — so this board is measuring cost, not faults. The same goes for `outcome=Rewarded` with an `error_kind` set: SPEC 4.2 requires that an ad failure never costs the player the reward, so that combination is expected.\n\n**There is no event for an ad the gate declined to show.** Suppressed interstitials are the normal case — a player inside the new-user grace generates one per level — and at that volume the funnel would be mostly noise. They log at debug and stay out of Loki. The one suppression worth counting is `outcome=granted_without_ad`, which is here, because it means a reward was paid for nothing.\n\n**`is_offline` on `ads.gate_shown` is the *device* signal**, not the app-wide banner one — our backend being down is not an ad-network outage. It is the one event whose own attribute deliberately shadows the per-record `is_offline` the export tree stamps.\n\n**Loki-backed, so nothing here can see past Grafana Cloud's log retention.** Widening the time picker does not widen the answer.\n\n**Delivery is at-least-once.** A record can rarely ship twice (export acknowledged, process died before the buffer delete), so read raw counts as approximate. Panels that count *installs* rather than records are immune to it by construction — a duplicate lands in the same `install_id` series and collapses.",
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 0,
  "links": [],
